.TH "si" "1" "2026\-10\-31" "(C) 2026" "General Commands Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
si \- parse, convert, and format physical quantities using SI units
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBsi\fR [OPTIONS] VALUE
.br
\fBsi\fR \-\-completions SHELL
.br
\fBsi\fR \-\-version
.br
\fBsi\fR \-\-help
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBsi\fR is a command\-line utility for parsing, converting, and formatting physical quantities expressed using the International System of Units (SI).\&
.PP
A quantity consists of a numeric value followed by a unit expression.\& 
Unit expressions support multiplication, division, exponentiation, and grouping using ASCII infix notation.\&
.PP
Quantities can be converted to a specified target unit, with dimensional compatibility checked during conversion.\&
Output can be formatted in several representations, including UTF\-8 encoded symbols, plain text, JSON, and LaTeX.\&
.PP
Numeric output supports configurable decimal precision and notation, including general, fixed\-point, scientific, and E\-notation.\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-notation\fR NOTATION
.RS 4
Set numeric notation.\& Supported values are \fBgeneral\fR, \fBfixed\fR, \fBscientific\fR, \fBe\fR, and \fBE\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR FORMAT
.RS 4
Set output format.\& Supported values are \fBpretty\fR, \fBplain\fR, \fBjson\fR, and \fBlatex\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-precision\fR INTEGER
.RS 4
Set decimal precision (default: 3).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-unit\fR UNIT
.RS 4
Convert the quantity to the specified target unit representation.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-strict\fR
.RS 4
Enforce strict parsing rules for quantities.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-completions\fR SHELL
.RS 4
Generate shell completions for Bash or Zsh.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Display version information.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Display help information.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH UNIT FORMAT EXPRESSIONS
.PP
Unit expressions use ASCII infix notation.\&
.nf
.RS 4
*	Multiplication
/	Division
^	Exponentiation
\-	Negative exponent
+	Positive exponent
()	Grouping
.fi
.RE
.PP
